 "description": "<p>Maniitsoq Airport (Greenlandic: Mittarfik Maniitsoq) (IATA: JSU, ICAO: BGMQ) is an airport located 0.5 NM (0.93 km; 0.58 mi) northwest[1] of Maniitsoq, a town in the Qeqqata municipality in central-western Greenland. It can serve STOL aircraft, although there is no deicing equipment at the airport, which is costly and problematic in Greenlandic winter. Source: <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maniitsoq_Airport\" target=\"_blank\">Wikipedia</a></p>",
